cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use tcpyPI, please cite both the peer-reviewed paper (preferred-citation
  below) and the software archive (the concept DOI, which always resolves to the
  latest version).
title: "tcpyPI (pyPI): Tropical Cyclone Potential Intensity Calculations in Python"
abstract: >-
  tcpyPI ('pyPI') computes and validates tropical cyclone potential intensity (PI)
  in Python. It is a documented, validated port of the Bister and Emanuel (2002)
  algorithm (originally FORTRAN, then MATLAB, by Kerry Emanuel), and includes
  utilities for PI log-decomposition and experimental TC diagnostics (ventilation
  index, genesis potential index, power dissipation index, relative intensity).
type: software
